P3. does a conservatism order exist on the overflow axis
model width W = 5, exhaustive over the whole representable domain

==========================================================================
unsigned F=0
  law                    wrap       saturate   exact    
  add_assoc              yes        yes        yes      
  add_identity           yes        yes        yes      
  add_monotone           .          yes        yes      
  distrib                yes        yes        yes      
  mul_assoc              yes        yes        yes      
  mul_identity           yes        yes        yes      
  mul_monotone_nonneg    .          yes        yes      
  mul_over_sub           yes        .          yes      
  top_absorbing          .          yes        .        
  zero_annihilates       yes        yes        yes      
  count                  7          9          9        

  fidelity against exact (lower is more faithful)
    wrap      wrong    1344 of    2048 ( 65.62%)  total abs err     247296  worst    960
    saturate  wrong    1344 of    2048 ( 65.62%)  total abs err     223173  worst    930
    exact     wrong       0 of    2048 (  0.00%)  total abs err          0  worst      0

  LAW ORDER, pairwise:
    wrap       vs saturate   : INCOMPARABLE
        only in wrap     : mul_over_sub
        only in saturate : add_monotone, mul_monotone_nonneg, top_absorbing
    wrap       vs exact      : wrap below exact
    saturate   vs exact      : INCOMPARABLE
        only in saturate : top_absorbing
        only in exact    : mul_over_sub

  FIDELITY ORDER, and it splits into two metrics that disagree:
    by frequency (how often the answer is wrong):
      wrap       vs saturate   : TIED, no order
      wrap       vs exact      : exact more faithful than wrap
      saturate   vs exact      : exact more faithful than saturate
    by magnitude (how far wrong the worst case is):
      wrap       vs saturate   : saturate more faithful than wrap
      wrap       vs exact      : exact more faithful than wrap
      saturate   vs exact      : exact more faithful than saturate

  VERDICT: the two candidate orders DISAGREE here. The law order makes
  wrapping and saturating incomparable, so a join over the law order
  does not exist, while the fidelity order ranks them. "The more
  conservative side" therefore has no referent at this predicate
  without saying which order is meant.

